\section*{T. Text v44: the check of text v43 and its LaTeX compile}
Sources: the read-only check \fn{writeup/lemmaU/bulk/fix25_check_v43/CHECK_v43.md} of text v43 (verdict ``OK with fixes''; no blocking finding; one should-fix item on records, five wording items, one note) and the LaTeX compile of text v43, \fn{writeup/lemmaU/bulk/fix26_latex_v43/LATEX_v43.md} (MiKTeX on the authors' Windows machine, in a scratch copy; all standalone documents compile once three source defects are worked around; the assembled step~3 has no error, no undefined reference, no undefined citation). Text v44 (\fn{writeup/lemmaU/bulk/fix27_texts_v44/}, built by \fn{tools/build_v44.py} from \fn{fix24_texts_v43/}, which is unchanged) applies both. No number was computed; no certified value changed; no Lean file was built or edited; nothing in the proof tree was run. Parts 1--7 above are verbatim; Part~8 (section S) is verbatim except for one sentence marked ``[Text v44, check fix25 F-2:]''.
\subsection*{T1. The check of text v43}
F-1 (records): \fn{TEXTS_REPORT_v43.md} \S1 (S-1) and \fn{TEXTS_LOG_v43.md} describe the first build of text v43, made before the raw logs of the S3 files existed. The final build of text v43 (24 November, 00:00; \fn{fix24_texts_v43/tools/build_v43.log}: ``S-1 compile logs on disk: True'') cites the three logs, and its numbers check reports two NEW-M38 rows, both the U-1 section number matched by value coincidence, not one. Both files belong to the closed text v43 and are not edited; the correction is recorded in \fn{RECORDS_ERRATA_v44.md}. F-2: section S above said that no Lean file was built; the three S3 files were recompiled per file to make the logs of S-1 (sources unchanged); corrected in place, marked. F-3: U-1 \S1.2 now says that the axiom checks cover the dependencies of the named theorems, not the whole import closure. F-4: the item ``Lean'' of the gaps list of C-1 now names the review of (PC), (MS), (GE) in \fn{fix23_delta_check/DELTA_CHECK_v42.md} Part~A. F-5: the U-1 lemma ``the Lean velocity is CDF'' is stated for the two cases that the Lean theorems cover: a $C^\infty$ map $\mathbb R\to\mathbb C$ with nonvanishing derivative on all of $\mathbb R$, and the lift of an immersion of \fn{Circle} read in a chart. F-6: \fn{main_v3_v44.tex}, step-3 caveat (b): (P1) rests on theorems compiled per file (full build and commit pending, status box) together with the [hand] steps of U-1 and C-1. Note: the Windows runs of both v4 kits (24 November 2026) are recorded in the open lists, in \fn{main_v3_v44.tex} \S``Independent reproduction'' and in \fn{step4_handoff_v44.tex}: \fn{kit3v4_run_win1/RUN_NOTES.md} (reproduces; the FAIL rows are CRLF-only differences of text outputs, the WARN rows last-bit float differences in diagnostic fields; two Windows-only kit bugs fixed in the run copy) and \fn{kit4bv4_run_win1/RUN_NOTES.md} (TOTAL PASS with 159 PASS, 0 FAIL, 1 WARN after four Windows-only fixes in the run copy). A kit v5 with these fixes is pending; no hash is cited for it.
\subsection*{T2. The LaTeX defects of text v43}
(1) \fn{key} was used but not defined in \fn{GS_lemma}, \fn{erratum} and \fn{flux2_lemma} (fatal); each now defines it with \fn{providecommand} and the body of \fn{lemmaU}'s definition. The macro check of texts v40--v43 missed it because it removed every \fn{key} argument together with the macro name before collecting the used names; \fn{tools/check_macros_v44.py} counts the wrapper macros \fn{fn}, \fn{key}, \fn{pth} as used, per standalone document, and fails on text v43. (2) The section title of the Lemma~U summary in \fn{step3_v44_main.tex} contained \fn{fn} with an underscore in its argument, which breaks when the table of contents is read back; it has a short title now. All sectioning and caption titles of the set were audited (\fn{tools/check_titles_v44.py}): the two titles of \fn{ei_lemma_v4c_v44.tex}, the caption of \fn{G1_export_k2_v44.tex} and the two captions of \fn{main_v3_v44.tex} that contain \fn{fn} also got short titles (they had compiled; starred titles take no short title and write nothing to the contents). (3) \fn{main_v3_v44.tex} needs \fn{fig_curves.pdf}; a copy of \fn{writeup/main/fig_curves.pdf} lies beside it in \fn{fix27_texts_v44/}. Also fixed: the provenance of \fn{numbers_A_v44.tex} in \fn{lemmaS_A_v44.tex} named a generator under \fn{fix17_texts_v39/} with a later version tag (a retag artefact of earlier builders); it now names \fn{fix27_texts_v44/tools/gen_numbers_A_v44.py}.
\subsection*{T3. Status (v44)}
Step~3 is \emph{not} closed. Done since section S: the LaTeX compile of text v43 (its defects fixed here); the Windows runs of both v4 kits. Open: the compile of text v44; kit v5 with the Windows-only fixes, and its runs; a full \fn{lake build CWFlow.Curve.All} and its log; the commit of \fn{CWFlow/Curve/} and its citation; the author items (P3$'$), Lemma~O arc by arc, the single-point statement; the step-4 text patch (\fn{STEP4_PATCH_NOTE_v44.md}, needs the authors' go); a final review. The text-v44 changes have not been checked independently.
